# xaubot strategy memory

This project copies `gold_trades` signals from Supabase (`pcieshmxxwplaodkrqet`) into MT5 (local or Windows VPS).

Current rules (2026-09-12):

- Poll every `POLL_SEC` seconds (default 5). Immediate scan on startup.
- New signal = `status=open` and `mt5_ticket` is null. Market order only: long=BUY, short=SELL.
- Filters live under `filters/` (one file each); `active_filters()` runs before open.
- First filter `israel_hours`: no new entries during Israel `[12:00,14:30)` and `[22:00,24:00)`.
- Second filter `london_after_ny`: from Israel `15:30` block `color=london`; allow `yellow` and `ny`.
- Third filter `us_holiday_next_day`: on next weekday after observed US holiday, new entries only until `10:00` IDT; open trades continue.
- Fourth filter `ny_open`: every day no new entries Israel `[15:20,15:30)` (NY cash open / fake liquidity).
- Guards before open: filters, `MAX_AGE_SEC`, `MAX_SLIP_USD`, `MAX_OPEN`, broker stops distance. Default `DRY_RUN=0` (live opens); set `1` only to simulate.
- Claim `copied_at` (null-only) before send to avoid double-open.
- SL/TP from the row. Fixed lot from `LOT_SIZE`. Symbol from `MT5_SYMBOL`.
- After fill: `mt5_ticket`, `copied_at`, `mt5_fill_price` (do not overwrite journal `entry`). On failure write `mt5_error` and clear claim.
- Lock 40/35 locally: `none → pend → locked`. Formula from webhook `entry`+`tp`. On closed M5 40% hit → pend. At start of next M5, if lock SL is on the wrong side of price, skip before clamp. Clamp stays at least `min_stop_distance×1.2` from market and never crosses `mt5_fill_price`. Then `set_sl`. Log symbol `stops_level` on bot start. `LOCK_ENABLE` default on.
- Track copied rows with `mt5_ticket` set, `mt5_closed_at` null, and `date_idt` within 7 days — not by `status`. Pine owns `status` / `exit` / `exit_reason` / `pips` / `usd_0_3`.
- On MT5 close write only `mt5_close_price`, `mt5_closed_at` (UTC), `mt5_profit`, `mt5_exit_reason`. `deal.time` is broker server clock; convert with a whole-hour offset from `tick.time`, reusing the last good offset when the tick is stale. Refuse close without an OUT deal for that position (`history_deals_get(position=ticket)` only).
- Each cycle log ORPHAN if an MT5 position (our magic) is outside that track (do not auto-close).
- Cutover 2026-09-21: before that date, rows with `mt5_ticket` have journal `exit`/`exit_reason` overwritten by MT5 and the original Pine values cannot be recovered. After that date those journal fields are Pine; broker truth is `mt5_*`. Rows with null `mt5_ticket` were always Pine.
- Gann/statics existence checks are cached in-process after a successful save (no repeat SELECT every poll).
- After connect/ensure: auto-enable MT5 Algo Trading toolbar if it is off.
- Do not generate signals. Do not size lots by risk. Do not trail/partial-close yet.
- Trade timestamps stay UTC; Israel TZ only for hour filters + Gann `date_idt`.
- After Israel 00:05, once per day write yesterday's aggregates to `gold_statics` (tp/sl/lock counts + profit/pips). Module `statics.py`.
- Each trading day write Gann grids to `gann_levels`. Do not open trades from those rows.
- After each successful `run_cycle`, write `heartbeat.txt` next to `bot.py` (UTC). `watchdog.ps1` restarts the bot if heartbeat is stale (~90s). Python from `.venv`, `WATCHDOG_PYTHON`, or gitignored `watchdog.local.ps1`. Entry script is a full path; Start-Bot redirects stdout/stderr to `bot_out.log`/`bot_err.log`.

## When the strategy changes

If the user changes, improves, or asks to change entry/exit, scan timing, lot, symbol, filters, or sync behavior, update **all three** in the same turn:

1. [STRATEGY.md](STRATEGY.md) — full rules + a dated changelog line
2. [MEMORY.md](MEMORY.md) — the "מצב נוכחי" snapshot
3. This rule — the "Current rules" bullets if execution rules changed

Do not leave these files stale after a strategy edit.
